  ('6a34ee00-d495-4635-9af9-6b4a7446d098','Driftless-area shooters passing through Sparta, Wisconsin have a local stop in B&L Archery Pro Shop, a commercial range serving the western part of the state. Beyond the name and location, current records are light, no confirmed lesson program, course layout, or lane count, so none of that should be assumed going in. The pro shop name hints at a retail side alongside the range itself, though that hasn''t been independently verified either. Anyone in the Sparta area wanting to shoot or browse gear should call ahead to B&L Archery Pro Shop to confirm current hours, pricing, and exactly what services are actually offered before making the trip.'),
  ('b089a4b4-3481-48cc-8488-25f5f9a3fab6','Pikes Peak-region archers have another option in BA Legend Archery, a commercial range in Colorado Springs joining the city''s handful of established shooting spots. Specifics like course type, lane count, and lesson availability aren''t confirmed in current records, so this profile is a starting point rather than a full picture of what''s on site. Colorado Springs sits in a part of the state with genuinely active bowhunting and target archery traditions thanks to nearby public land, giving a new commercial entrant a built-in audience. Anyone considering BA Legend Archery should check current listings or call directly to confirm hours, pricing, and what''s actually available before making the drive.'),
  ('f35e2bc9-45e6-4c30-b91c-7e488d5714c2','Back 80 Bowshooters serves shooters around Cherokee, in Oklahoma''s rural north-central plains. There isn''t much on file yet beyond the name and location, no confirmed course type, lesson program, or lane count, making this more a starting point than a complete profile. Rural northern Oklahoma has a solid bowhunting tradition, and clubs like this one typically run on member involvement rather than paid staff, which usually means a shoot schedule built around the group''s own calendar rather than posted business hours. Anyone in the Cherokee area interested in joining should reach out directly to Back 80 Bowshooters to ask about membership, meeting times, and what the range currently offers.'),
  ('084f721f-a12e-4e6a-b6e3-6bfeb47b5a28','Tucked into North Carolina''s Piedmont between Durham and Hillsborough, Back Creek Bow Hunters serves archers around Efland. The public record doesn''t yet confirm specifics like course layout, lesson availability, or lane count, so consider this a starting point rather than a full profile. A club carrying "bow hunters" in its name typically leans toward bowhunting-style practice, foam targets and natural terrain rather than a formal indoor lane setup, though that''s an inference from the name and not an independently confirmed feature. Piedmont-area archers interested in joining or visiting should contact Back Creek Bow Hunters directly to confirm membership terms, meeting schedule, and what the course actually looks like on the ground.'),
  ('09a1fa49-12c1-40d0-b0d5-eb908e2b8f15','Eleven lanes and a genuine lesson program set Back Room Archery Shop apart from a bare-bones California range, with an attached pro shop rounding out the operation for customers who want to handle equipment or pick up supplies during the same visit. That combination of confirmed lane count, coaching, and retail points to a full-service setup built for beginners and regulars alike, not just a place to rent time on a lane. The specific city isn''t confirmed in current records, so California archers interested in Back Room Archery Shop should look up its exact location and current lesson schedule directly before planning a visit.'),
  ('8d413de5-b2e4-425f-85fb-40888bea001c','Near Maryland''s western panhandle, close to the West Virginia line, Backwoods Archery serves the Clear Spring area as a local club. Specifics on course type, lessons, or lane count aren''t confirmed in the public record yet, so this listing marks a starting point rather than a full rundown of what''s on site. Western Maryland''s ridges and wooded public land make it solid country for the kind of outdoor 3D or field-style shooting many small regional clubs favor, though that''s regional context rather than a confirmed feature of this specific club. Panhandle-area archers interested in Backwoods Archery should reach out directly to ask about membership, meeting times, and the kind of range the club maintains.'),
  ('c239f954-7b21-4e70-a43e-77797cba484f','A commercial range and pro shop under the name Badass Archery serves Sandy, part of the dense Salt Lake Valley archery scene along Utah''s Wasatch Front. Having a shop on site means customers can handle bows, get equipment serviced, or pick up supplies during the same trip they come to shoot, rather than treating the range and retail as separate errands. Beyond that, current records don''t confirm course type, lesson availability, or lane count, so those remain open questions. Sandy sits within easy reach of several other Salt Lake-area ranges, so archers comparing options should call Badass Archery directly to find out what actually sets its course and shop apart.'),
  ('8198ad55-fe36-4e7d-aa86-72c3ab32f974','Ranching and hunting country in Montana''s Beaverhead Valley is where Badger Archery operates, a commercial range in Dillon that pairs an on-site pro shop with lessons. That combination fills a real need in a region where bowhunting is a serious pastime, giving beginners a place to learn fundamentals and experienced shooters a place to restock gear without leaving town. The lesson offering suggests Badger Archery is built for newcomers as much as for archers who already know their way around a bow. Anyone in the Beaverhead County area wanting instruction or equipment should contact Badger Archery directly to confirm current lesson availability, pricing, and shop hours.'),
  ('60c0c73e-1d58-4690-b7ae-cae8e35c2dc8','Banana Bend Archery Club serves Baytown, an industrial Gulf Coast city east of Houston along the Houston Ship Channel. Public records don''t yet confirm the club''s course type, lesson offerings, or lane count, so this listing is a starting point rather than a full profile of what''s on site. With another archery club also based in Baytown according to current listings, the area supports a genuinely active local archery community despite its industrial reputation. Anyone in the Baytown or greater Houston area curious about Banana Bend Archery Club should reach out directly to ask about membership requirements, meeting schedule, and what kind of shooting the club offers.'),
  ('d1860f12-9256-4ad4-90b9-6c75f2f4f2f6','A confirmed 3D archery course sets Baraboo Bowmen apart from a plain open-lane setup, maintained in Baraboo, in Wisconsin''s scenic Baraboo Hills near Devil''s Lake State Park. Foam targets placed through varied terrain reward accurate distance judgment, the kind of practice bowhunters lean on heavily ahead of Wisconsin''s deer season. Beyond the course itself, current records don''t confirm lesson availability or lane count, so those remain open questions for now. South-central Wisconsin archers interested in 3D shooting should contact Baraboo Bowmen directly to ask about membership, course access, and the shoot schedule before making the trip out.')
